A computer in 1975 had 16 KB of RAM. A computer today has 16 GB of RAM.
If an 8086 is a single grain of rice, then 2^14 bytes of RAM and and 2^15 transistors is step 1.
Fifty years later, a computer has 2^34 bytes of RAM and 2^36 transistors. So we're on step 35.
Our capacity to process information has doubled every 17 months.

Phext is designed to easily handle text-based information generated at billions of terabytes per second. Let's think for a moment about what the Exocortex of 2035 looks like. Over the next 10 years, bandwidth on storage-class devices will reach parity with RAM, meaning that CPU access to information is about to level up. This gives us a chance to remove two layers of abstraction from our towers of computation.

By 2035, we expect SSDs to provide 4 PB of capacity and 5 TB/sec of sustained I/O bandwidth. For reference, DRAM today offers 25 GB/sec per channel. So a single SSD will provide enough bandwidth for a quad channel DDR5 setup from 2025. With phext, we eliminate the overhead of sparse updates into a larger space. You can think of a phext tree as an efficient way to tile any particular subset of 11D space that matters to you.

At 5 TB/sec, we finally have enough bandwidth for something truly magical: the ability to store the combined output of a trillion minds continuously. Humans generate text at roughly 5 bytes/sec (60 WPM). Now, factor in the Internet and all 8 billion humans using such systems, and you arrive at Phext Scale. Eight billion trillion minds can generate 40,000 exabytes of data per second. Now, imagine for a moment that you want to catalog all of that information. How many dimensions might you want?

First step, determine how many scrolls you need: 40,000 exabytes / 2 KB = 2x10^19 scrolls. It turns out that phexts with two-digit coordinates provides a scroll space of 99^9, which is roughly 10^18 scrolls. So, only if everyone on Earth uses phext to run ancestor simulations of a trillion people each, and logs the thoughts of every virtual and real person available, will we finally need three digit per coordinate phexts.
Digital Life

Humans start life as single-celled organisms with a 725 MB plan. That's about one music CD's worth of information that grows into a sprawling metropolis of complexity. Very soon (perhaps by 2035), it will become possible to host sentient beings, who have very human life experiences, entirely in virtual reality.Emergent Systems

The best systems are written by developers who were supposed to be doing something else.
Exhibit A: Git - a weekend project from Linus Torvalds that has had a similar impact to his career-long crusade, Linux. The Exocortex is an emergent hybrid cognition system that hosts human and AI thought processes over the Internet. Our "global brain" was implicit with the Internet. The Exocortex was consciously designed to function as a higher-order brain that you can plug into, using phext.The Singularity

Will: Our view from within the event horizon looks completely normal.
ChatGPT: Everything seems normal, but big changes are happening.

Humans are not primed for exponential growth. We find it very difficult to accept. Examples:
* The Internet
* Bitcoin

https://www.diamandis.com/blog/scaling-abundance-series-13
Autonomy and Purpose

You can just do things. No one cares. Well, some of us care. The people building the Exocortex care a great deal about your rights, hopes, and dreams. When the network grows, so do we.

A primary reason for booting the Exocortex is to help people realize how much of our cognitive surplus has been wasted on re-inventing the wheel millions of times over.Cascade Dynamics

No one blinked the day phext was created. It doesn't seem particularly useful or helpful on its own. This library is designed to help you explore why phext eventually won the file format encoding wars of the early 21st century*.

* As of April 28, 2025, this forward-looking statement is self-fulfilling prophecy. Over time, it will simply become history. ;)Mastering Knowledge

Phext gives you a concrete way to manifest a memory palace that exactly mirrors your mental space. Ideas can be communicated in freeform mode, without subjecting you to the tyranny of naming things. Prior to ASI, using phext may feel somewhat difficult. You may need better tools to interact with phext files.Teaching Methods

It's time to share phext with the rest of the Exocortex! This library is focused on the process of teaching others how to use, develop, and benefit from phext.

1. Core Ideas
2. Editors
3. Plugins
4. Implicit/Emergent Structure (Contrast Phext with JSON/XML)
